     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all<div><br></div><div>This Fall the Stats Camp is coming to California, with 3 day courses. <span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">We have a register now, pay later option so folks can reserve a seat. The URL for the fall camp is:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"> </span><a href=\"https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__www.statscamp.org_fall-2Dcamp_&amp;d=DwMFAg&amp;c=S1d2Gs1Y1NQV8Lx35_Qi5FnTH2uYWyh_OhOS94IqYCo&amp;r=YjdBtnf8LkLLcph3uDej4yPlM-OYnqhJIOLDc94Bmvr-FMi1GhVi50uqK3ALNJIo&amp;m=5FHIhz8dRc8VyLhxGbFVr9zrPf9RSO07c4CoBcTBMIw&amp;s=0Lehdr3YakD8wvWbiKA6Z4eK9-IXK-iMnEtsA7Tes7M&amp;e=\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u%3Dhttps-3A__www.statscamp.org_fall-2Dcamp_%26d%3DDwMFAg%26c%3DS1d2Gs1Y1NQV8Lx35_Qi5FnTH2uYWyh_OhOS94IqYCo%26r%3DYjdBtnf8LkLLcph3uDej4yPlM-OYnqhJIOLDc94Bmvr-FMi1GhVi50uqK3ALNJIo%26m%3D5FHIhz8dRc8VyLhxGbFVr9zrPf9RSO07c4CoBcTBMIw%26s%3D0Lehdr3YakD8wvWbiKA6Z4eK9-IXK-iMnEtsA7Tes7M%26e%3D&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463629401000&amp;usg=AOvVaw284lu6rblxD9hz6i0uNVQk\">https://www.statscamp.org/fall-camp/</a></div><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Statistics Course Offerings in Orange County:</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Applied Latent Class Analysis (LCA) Course</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">– Instructor, Katherine Masyn, Ph.D.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">This is an intermediate 3-day course introducing latent class analysis with categorical, cross-sectional data using Mplus.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Bayesian Data Analysis Course</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">– Instructor, Mauricio Garnier-Villarreal, Ph.D.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">An introductory 3-day course about Bayesian Data Analysis, focus on the differences to the frequentist approach, and application of several models</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Item Response Theory (IRT) Course</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">– Instructor, Steve Reise, Ph.D.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">This is an introductory 3-day course introducing item response theory measurement models applied to psychological and educational data.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Longitudinal Structural Equation Modeling (SEM) Course</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">– Instructor, Todd Little, Ph.D.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">This is an intermediate 3-day Stats Camp course introducing Longitudinal Structural Equation Modeling.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Missing Data Analysis Course</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">– Instructor, Craig Enders, Ph.D.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">This is an intermediate 3-day course introducing multiple imputation and maximum likelihood estimation for missing data.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">Psychometrics Course</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">– Instructor, Larry Price, Ph.D.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\">This is an introductory 3-day course in the foundations of psychometrics. Participants should be proficient specific to the material covered in a two-semester graduate-level social science statistics course sequence.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"> </p></div>"
